<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28807" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕrīdĭo</span></b> ,
		1, v. n., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕrīdĭor</span></b> , 1,
			v. dep.
		meridies, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to take a mid-day nap</i> or <i>siesta</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jube, ad te veniam meridiatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					32, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">meridiari ante cibum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
					2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dum ea meridiaret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter acervos eorum meridiati sunt,</span>”
				i. e. <i>have taken their ease</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Job, 24, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
